lass VR environment, the Physician can trigger SciX queries via voice command (e.g., “SciX: Show similar activation patterns in recent epilepsy studies”), with the results appearing as floating windows next to the live 3D brain model.","position":{"start":{"line":62,"column":1},"end":{"line":62,"column":1}},"key":"LZXS6wn8q0"}],"key":"a06LYI8BxE"}],"key":"Te7xFJf8T2"}],"key":"QYCLMH2h4G"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"“Sensory Re-Calibration”","position":{"start":{"line":64,"column":1},"end":{"line":64,"column":1}},"key":"osLhHT83zx"}],"identifier":"sensory-re-calibration","label":"“Sensory Re-Calibration”","html_id":"sensory-re-calibration","implicit":true,"key":"Xr2YeV7JCJ"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tactile Mapping: If a user has lost sensation in a limb, the Physician can use syGlass in XR to manually stimulate specific “dead” zones. By “tapping” a virtual neuron in the XR environment, they send a signal to the NESD to trigger a phantom touch for the user.","position":{"start":{"line":65,"column":1},"end":{"line":65,"column":1}},"key":"b9x0bkMckM"}],"key":"Y3tFxxPRUC"}],"key":"XKLadw15mV"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pain Suppression: The Physician can identify “pain circuits” (hyper-active clusters) and use an XR interface to “dim” those regions, sending inhibitory signals to provide immediate relief.","position":{"start":{"line":66,"column":1},"end":{"line":66,"column":1}},"key":"LQksy1z4Rv"}],"key":"gok8W8Q9wJ"}],"key":"WhDMGcMURI"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":68,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SciX Integration: During manipulation, SciX provides real-time “Safety Envelopes.” If the Physician tries to stimulate a region too intensely, SciX flags a clinical study or safety protocol as a HUD overlay in the XR headset.","position":{"start":{"line":67,"column":1},"end":{"line":67,"column":1}},"key":"lJYSgkROnT"}],"key":"xaVNSUkRGZ"}],"key":"oomN1rn41w"}],"key":"cildWTtpHn"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Technical Implementation via syGlass & SciStream","position":{"start":{"line":69,"column":1},"end":{"line":69,"column":1}},"key":"wmPIYQhVrE"}],"identifier":"technical-implementation-via-syglass-scistream","label":"Technical Implementation via syGlass & SciStream","html_id":"technical-implementation-via-syglass-scistream","implicit":true,"key":"h1AN3mjMrW"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"spread":false,"position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":73,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Haptic Mirroring: Use the syGlass Python API to map XR controller coordinates to the 3D coordinates of the neural implant’s electrode array.","position":{"start":{"line":70,"column":1},"end":{"line":70,"column":1}},"key":"YIaeKfwmXd"}],"key":"OtP2v2clhd"}],"key":"pxh6smr7gx"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":71,"column":1},"end":{"line":71,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Latent Feedback (SciStream): To avoid “sensory lag” (which causes nausea or seizures), SciStream must maintain a sub-10ms round-trip latency between the XR “click” and the neural stimulation.","